The proliferation of seismic attributes is associated with the period starting in the mid-1960s, as indicated by the development of multifold data and interval velocity computations during this time. Additionally, the late 1960s saw geophysicists noticing strong isolated reflections and changes in reflection character, which later formed the foundation of seismic stratigraphy in 1975. Source: gsgpy_70_5_3SO.pdf — pages 3, 4. 

