The timeline illustrates the development of seismic attributes in relation to key advances in seismic exploration technology. It highlights significant milestones, such as the introduction of digital recording of seismic data in the 1960s, the presentation of complex trace analysis in the 1970s, and the classification of attributes in the 1990s. The timeline also shows the evolution of attribute analysis from seismic stratigraphy toward exploitation and reservoir characterization, particularly with the association of attributes with 3D seismic data. Source: gsgpy_70_5_3SO.pdf — page 3.

